==============================================================
POC: AI Creative Studio — Proof of Concept
Goal: Prove that the core loop works BEFORE building anything else
Definition of success: A user opens the desktop app, types a prompt,
and receives a generated image/video — powered by a shared Flow account
via your backend proxy.
==============================================================

You are a senior full-stack developer. Build a minimal POC with 3 parts:
  1. A simple Node.js/Express backend API (proxy to Flow)
  2. A minimal Electron desktop app (prompt → result)
  3. A single HTML page (register + get API key)

DO NOT build: payments, admin panel, credit system, email, Android app,
auto-updater, or any non-essential feature.

==============================================================
POC PART 1 — BACKEND API (Node.js + Express)
==============================================================

Stack: Node.js 20 + Express + Redis (BullMQ queue) + axios + playwright

Folder structure:
/poc-backend
  server.js          -- Express app entry
  routes/
    auth.js          -- POST /api/validate-key
    generate.js      -- POST /api/generate/image, POST /api/generate/video
    jobs.js          -- GET /api/jobs/:id
  services/
    flowProxy.js     -- The core: maintains Flow session + makes requests
    queue.js         -- BullMQ queue setup
    sessionKeeper.js -- Cron: keeps Flow session alive every 10 min
  middleware/
    keyAuth.js       -- Validates X-License-Key header
  db.js              -- SQLite (use 'better-sqlite3', no MySQL needed for POC)
  .env.example
  package.json

--- DATABASE (SQLite for POC — no MySQL setup needed) ---

Table: poc_users
  id, email, license_key (random 32-char hex), is_active, created_at

Table: poc_jobs
  id (uuid), user_id, type (image/video), prompt,
  status (queued/processing/completed/failed),
  output_url, error, created_at, updated_at

Seed 1 test user with a known license key for POC testing.
Example: key = "poc-test-key-12345678"

--- FLOW PROXY SERVICE (flowProxy.js) — MOST CRITICAL FILE ---

IMPORTANT: This service has TWO possible implementations.
Implement BOTH and switch between them via env var FLOW_MODE.

FLOW_MODE=api (if Flow has a REST API):
  - Store FLOW_API_KEY in .env
  - Make direct HTTP requests to Flow's API endpoints
  - No browser automation needed
  - Headers: { Authorization: "Bearer {FLOW_API_KEY}" }

FLOW_MODE=browser (if Flow requires browser session):
  - Use Playwright (npm install playwright)
  - On startup: launch headless Chromium, navigate to flow.so, log in
    using FLOW_EMAIL + FLOW_PASSWORD from .env
  - Store cookies/session after login
  - On each generation request: use the stored session to make the
    generation request programmatically
  - Keep session alive: ping flow.so/api/ping (or equivalent) every 10 min

INVESTIGATION STEP (do this BEFORE implementing either mode):
  Add a script: scripts/investigateFlow.js
  This script opens Playwright with headful (visible) browser,
  logs into Flow with the provided credentials, then:
  - Logs ALL network requests to console (request URL + method + body)
  - Waits 60 seconds (developer manually generates something in Flow)
  - Logs the response of the generation request
  Output: the exact API endpoint, headers, and payload Flow uses internally.
  Run with: node scripts/investigateFlow.js
  Developer MUST run this first and update flowProxy.js accordingly.

Queue system (REQUIRED — prevents concurrent Flow session conflicts):
  Use BullMQ with Redis.
  All generation requests go into a single queue: "generation-queue"
  Concurrency: 1 (one job at a time — shared Flow account cannot handle parallel)
  On job complete: update poc_jobs table, store output_url

--- API ENDPOINTS ---

POST /api/validate-key
  Body: { "license_key": "abc..." }
  Logic: Look up key in poc_users where is_active=1
  Response 200: {
    valid: true,
    user: { email: "user@test.com" },
    subscription: {
      status: "active",
      expires_at: "2026-05-01",
      days_remaining: 37,
      badge: "MONTHLY ACCESS"
    }
  }
  Response 401: { valid: false, error: "INVALID_KEY" }

POST /api/generate/image
  Header: X-License-Key: {key}
  Body: { prompt: string, model: "default", aspect_ratio: "16:9" }
  Middleware: keyAuth.js validates key first
  Logic:
    1. Create job in poc_jobs with status=queued
    2. Add to BullMQ queue
    3. Return { job_id, status: "queued" }

POST /api/generate/video
  Header: X-License-Key: {key}
  Body: { prompt: string, duration: 8, quality: "fast" }
  Same pattern as image — different Flow endpoint

GET /api/jobs/:id
  Header: X-License-Key: {key}
  Logic: fetch job from poc_jobs, return current status + output_url if done
  Poll every 3s from frontend until status = completed or failed

--- MIDDLEWARE: keyAuth.js ---
  Extract X-License-Key from request headers
  Query SQLite: SELECT * FROM poc_users WHERE license_key = ? AND is_active = 1
  If found: attach user to req.user, call next()
  If not found: return 401 { error: "UNAUTHORIZED" }

--- SESSION KEEPER (sessionKeeper.js) ---
  Run on app startup using node-cron
  Every 10 minutes: call a lightweight Flow endpoint to keep session alive
  If session expires (401 from Flow): re-login automatically using stored credentials
  Log session status to console

--- .env.example ---
PORT=3001
FLOW_MODE=browser         # or "api"
FLOW_EMAIL=your@email.com
FLOW_PASSWORD=yourpassword
FLOW_API_KEY=             # if FLOW_MODE=api
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
JWT_SECRET=any-random-string

==============================================================
POC PART 2 — ELECTRON DESKTOP APP
==============================================================

Stack: Electron 28 + React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS
Distribution: portable target (single .exe, no installer, no code signing)
electron-builder config: win.target = "portable"

Folder structure:
/poc-electron
  src/
    main/
      main.js          -- Electron entry, creates BrowserWindow
      preload.js       -- Context bridge: exposes ipcRenderer safely
    renderer/
      App.jsx          -- Root React component, routing
      pages/
        AuthPage.jsx   -- Key entry screen
        DashboardPage.jsx  -- Choose: Image or Video
        ImagePage.jsx  -- Image generation UI
        VideoPage.jsx  -- Video generation UI
      store/
        appStore.js    -- Zustand: licenseKey, user, subscription
      api.js           -- All backend calls (axios, base URL from env)
  electron-builder.yml
  vite.config.js
  package.json

