--- api.js (all backend calls) ---
const BASE = process.env.API_URL || 'http://localhost:3001'

export const validateKey = (key) =>
  axios.post(`${BASE}/api/validate-key`, { license_key: key })

export const generateImage = (key, body) =>
  axios.post(`${BASE}/api/generate/image`, body, {
    headers: { 'X-License-Key': key }
  })

export const generateVideo = (key, body) =>
  axios.post(`${BASE}/api/generate/video`, body, {
    headers: { 'X-License-Key': key }
  })

export const pollJob = (key, jobId) =>
  axios.get(`${BASE}/api/jobs/${jobId}`, {
    headers: { 'X-License-Key': key }
  })

==============================================================
POC PART 3 — MINIMAL WEBSITE (single HTML file)
==============================================================

Single file: /poc-website/index.html
No framework. Pure HTML + Tailwind CDN.

Pages (show/hide with JS, no routing):
  1. Landing: headline + "Get POC Access" button → shows register form
  2. Register form: name + email + submit → POST /api/register → shows key
  3. Key display: "Your API License Key: [key]" + copy button + download app link

Backend addition for website: add to server.js
  POST /api/register
    Body: { name, email }
    Logic: generate random 32-char hex key, insert into poc_users
    Response: { license_key: "abc123..." }

==============================================================
POC SUCCESS CRITERIA (test these in order)
==============================================================
1. Run: node server.js → backend starts on port 3001, no errors
2. Open poc-website/index.html in browser → register → get a key
3. Run Electron app → enter the key → see DashboardPage
4. Click "Open" on Image card → type a prompt → hit send
5. See skeleton loading → then see an actual generated image
6. Click "Open" on Video card → type a prompt → hit send
7. See "Generating..." → then see a playable video
8. All 7 steps pass = POC is proven = proceed to full build

